
  <sn><md>### What Regex *Is*

![img](https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20251220171423685683/example_of_regular_expression.webp)

A **regular expression** is a `compact notation` for describing **regular languages** — sets of strings that can be recognized by a finite automaton. At its core, regex is **pattern matching**: it answers the question *"does this string contain a substring of this shape?"*

Formally, regex engines correspond to one of:

- **Finite automata** (true "regular" languages) — regular expressions in the theoretical CS sense
- **Backtracking engines with extensions** (PCRE, Python `re`, JavaScript) — these add features (backreferences, lookaround, recursion) that go *beyond* regular languages
</md></sn>
